ames (R) in Michigan's 10th Congressional District", "source": "Ballotpedia News", "published": "2026-06-16T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 3.24, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": -1.5, "poll_sd": 14.68, "poll_weight": 0.11, "fundamentals": {"margin": 5.17, "lean": -3.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -0.03}, "rating_margin": 1.94, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.27, "baseline_margin": 2.72, "analyst_adjustment": -0.22, "key_factors": ["Open Republican-leaning seat (R+3) in a strongly Democratic midterm environment", "Prediction markets price Hines near a two-in-three chance", "Raters split between Tossup (Cook, Sabato, DDHQ, Fox) and Lean D (Economist, Silver Bulletin, Split Ticket, FPO)", "Bouchard's large cash-on-hand edge versus Hines's outside-spending advantage; the lone recent poll is tied"], "rationale": "An open R+3 seat in a favorable Democratic midterm environment gives Hines a modest edge, corroborated by markets pricing her near two-in-three and four of nine raters calling it Lean Democratic. Bouchard's cash advantage and the single tied August poll keep this at the soft end of Lean D.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling or a late wave of Republican outside spending behind Bouchard could pull the race back to Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: John James (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 10th District is an open seat after Republican John James left the House to run for governor. The district leans Republican by about three points, but the 2026 midterm environment favors Democrats, making the seat genuinely contested. Christina Hines won the Democratic nomination while Mike Bouchard, the longtime Oakland County sheriff, took the Republican side.\n\nBetting markets give Hines roughly a two-in-three chance, and several independent raters call the race Lean Democratic, though Cook, Sabato, and others rate it a Tossup and Inside Elections tilts Republican. The only recent public poll, from mid-August, showed the candidates tied. Bouchard holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, while Democratic outside groups have outspent Republican ones on Hines's behalf. The evidence points to a narrow Democratic edge in a race that could easily go the other way.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6628, "margin": 2.54}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6491, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6831, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.623, "margin": 2.5}]}